# HeartThreshold rules

Source documents (read before making changes):
- @docs/ARCHITECTURE.md — WHAT to build and the non-negotiable rules. Wins any conflict.
- @docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md — WHEN/in what order. Work only on the current phase.

Non-negotiables:
- The watch decides alerts AND records the session. No alert logic in TypeScript; the phone never edits samples.
- Apple Watch: HKWorkoutSession + HKLiveWorkoutBuilder, activityType .other, locationType .indoor,
  heart rate only, Workout processing background mode.
- Record every heart-rate sample with its timestamp; never down-sample on the watch.
  Append to disk at least every 60 s (buffered); never rewrite whole files mid-session.
- Support sessions up to 10 hours: workout recovery, interrupted finalization, battery guard (default 10%),
  wrist-down display updates at most once per minute. Alerts still evaluate every sample.
- Never fabricate or interpolate heart-rate data; gaps are shown as gaps.
- Phone ↔ Apple Watch only via WatchConnectivity through the `watch-bridge` native module.
  Recordings: transferFile at session end; native module moves the file to the inbox before returning, then acks.
  Settings (later phase): updateApplicationContext. Never App Groups for cross-device data. Nothing per-sample.
- React Native screens import only the `WatchBridge` interface, never a platform adapter directly.
- Watch source lives in apps/mobile/targets/watch. Never hand-edit generated `ios/`; use Expo config.
- ThresholdEngine, SummaryCalculator and TS aggregation must pass the vectors in contracts/.
- Validate every payload crossing a device or network boundary. Field names come from contracts/.
- Watch-generated UUIDs are primary keys everywhere (idempotent import/sync).
- No backend before Phase 11. The watch never calls the network or Supabase.
- No fake sensor data outside tests/previews. Never swallow HealthKit, workout, file or transfer errors.
- Wellness wording only; never claim diagnosis or emergency monitoring.

Working style:
- Small, testable types. TypeScript strict. Swift async/await; UI on main actor.
- At the end of a task, list which "Done when" checks for the current phase now pass and which need a physical device.
- After watch or phone source changes, build and install without being asked. Build the HeartThreshold scheme for the connected iPhone (`-allowProvisioningUpdates`), then install `Debug-watchos/watch.app` on the paired Apple Watch and launch `com.justcabyr.heartthreshold.watchkitapp`. Install the iPhone app too when phone source changed.
